{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "title": "Ecco Studio master size roster",
  "approval": "2026-11-08: User approved these sizes through the size audit, two rounds of before/after mockups of 24 screens and per-row decisions. Element types are sized here once; every instance of a type takes these values.",
  "howItWorks": [
    "Each entry is an element type. Its selectors decide which elements belong to it; font, height and width are applied to every match by design-system/sizes.css.",
    "Entries are applied in order. When an element matches several entries, the later entry wins, so variants and more specific types come after general ones.",
    "Edit this file, then run: python3 scripts/size_roster.py. Never edit design-system/sizes.css by hand.",
    "A new element whose type is already here needs no size of its own. A new kind of element must be added here (a new type or a variant) in the same change; the ROSTER-01 browser check fails otherwise.",
    "Types marked keptCurrent keep the size they had before the roster existed; they are listed so they can be edited like any other type."
  ],
  "units": "Numbers are CSS pixels. A string is used as-is (for example a kept original size such as calc(15px - 2pt)). null leaves that property to the element's own styles.",
  "types": [
